# OpenClaw — Legal AI Operating Layer (Vertical v1)

## What This Is

The Legal AI Operating Layer is the **first proof-of-concept vertical** built on the OpenClaw factory framework. It validates the repeatable pattern: dataset → training → eval → registry → deployment → governed endpoints.

It is NOT the product. It is the demonstration that the factory works.

## Live Endpoints

All under `/api/v1/legal/`:

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/v1/legal/extract-clause` | POST | Classify contract clause into 5 types |
| `/v1/legal/extract-clause` | GET | Asset info + lineage + eval results |
| `/v1/legal/intake` | POST | Matter classification + routing |
| `/v1/legal/contract/analyze` | POST | Contract specialist |
| `/v1/legal/litigation/analyze` | POST | Litigation specialist |
| `/v1/legal/ip/analyze` | POST | IP specialist |
| `/v1/legal/employment/analyze` | POST | Employment specialist |
| `/v1/legal/corporate/analyze` | POST | Corporate governance specialist |
| `/v1/legal/next-asset-baseline` | POST | Run baseline eval for next asset |

## Clause Taxonomy

5 clause types supported:
- `governing_law` — jurisdiction specification
- `termination` — contract termination conditions
- `ip_assignment` — IP ownership/transfer
- `limitation_of_liability` — damage caps
- `indemnification` — loss compensation obligations

